paragraph('Candidate and admission observations are available for C, D, and E,',r'Candidate and admission observations are available for C, D, and E, with target-specific gaps. ProFTPD lacks these observations in D and E despite nonzero model usage. No provisional-lifecycle or repair-outcome observations are available across the 642 records. Reported provisional counts for admission, conversion, and expiration are zero throughout; the rates in \namedref{Table}{tab:mechanisms} therefore describe recorded counters, not verified queue behavior. \namedref{Table}{tab:observed_log_counts} gives D-condition counts, and \namedref{Table}{tab:archive_arms} gives endpoint results. Missing observations establish neither zero conversion rates nor absence of provisional validation or repair.')
paragraph('Reported dispositions do not independently establish durable queue membership.',r'Recorded dispositions do not independently verify durable queue membership. Without validated candidate-to-descendant links and a paired C--D comparison, promotion latency, downstream productivity, nonproductive retention, and admission false negatives cannot be estimated. Unreconciled usage also prevents attributing code gain to individual candidates or token expenditure. Accordingly, no reduction in queue pollution or improvement in downstream productivity or cost efficiency is claimed. \namedref{Table}{tab:mechanisms} and \namedref{Figure}{fig:dispositions} report observed decisions and latency descriptively; first-failure flags do not independently explain queue retention.')
replace(r'\subsection{RQ3: Scheduling evidence and unfilled causal results}',r'\subsection{RQ3: Exploratory scheduling diagnostics}')
replace(r'An equal-energy subset provides the only strictly comparable episode slice and fills the corresponding rows of \namedref{Table}{tab:mechanisms}.',r'An exploratory equal-energy subset holds the recorded mutation count constant for the corresponding diagnostics in \namedref{Table}{tab:mechanisms}; it does not establish matched target composition, run conditions, or a causal scheduling contrast.')
replace('Code-branch gain per episode & 0.009','Recorded code-edge gain / episode & 0.009')
